The '''Progressive Party of Okaiken''' ({{Nihongo|岡井県新法党|Okaiken Shinpōtō|}}), commonly known as the '''PPO''' ({{lang|ja|新法党}}, ''Shinpōtō''), is one of the two major political parties in [[Okaiken]]. It is a social democratic and centre-left party.

Founded in 1952, the PPO has long been the primary opposition to the conservative [[Liberal Democratic Party (Okaiken)|LDP]]. Since 2021, the PPO has been the largest party in the [[House of Commoners of Okaiken|House of Commoners]].

The current leader of the party is [[Honda Shigetsuma]], who also serves as the incumbent [[Prime Minister of Okaiken]]. The PPO currently governs as the senior partner in a coalition with the [[Okaiken Socialist Party|Okaiken Socialist Party (OSP)]].

==History==

===Founding and Early Years (1950s–1960s)===
The Progressive Party was founded on April 14, 1952, during the final year of the Shaydian occupation. It was formed by a coalition of moderate socialists, liberal reformers, and trade unionists who sought to create a strong centre-left alternative to the pre-war conservative establishment and the more radical [[Sanese Communist Party|Communist Party]].

Throughout the 1950s and 60s, the PPO was a major force in post-war politics, often trading power with the conservative Democratic Party. The party achieved its first period of government in 1961 under the leadership of '''[[Tadashige Honda]]''', a member of the prominent Honda family. His government was known for its "aggressive economic policies" and social platform.

During the [[Quiet Revolution]] (1967–1968), the PPO was part of the opposition that boycotted the Diet in protest of Socialist Prime Minister [[Genzui Kusaka]]'s attempts to abolish parliament. The party played a key role in the political realignment that followed, which led to the establishment of the Mitoyagi Republic in 1970.

===Era of LDP Dominance (1970s–1990s)===
Following the 1977 realignment that formed the modern [[Liberal Democratic Party (Okaiken)|LDP]], the PPO found itself as the primary party of opposition. For most of the 1970s and 1980s, the party was shut out of power as the LDP oversaw the "Sanese Recovery" and the "Go-go 8090" economic bubble.

The PPO's fortunes changed in 1990. The LDP's popularity collapsed following the [[Miyazaki hotel scandal]], and the PPO, now led by '''[[Shigehara Honda]]''' (brother of Tadashige Honda), successfully formed a broad, multi-party coalition. Honda's election as Prime Minister broke decades of LDP dominance and marked the first non-LDP government since the 1970s. This coalition was briefly ousted in 1991 but quickly returned to power, with Honda serving again until 1993.

The LDP returned to power in 1993 and, with the exception of the PPO's brief 1990-1993 governments, the PPO remained the main opposition party for the next two decades.

===Return to Government (2016–Present)===
The PPO, now led by '''[[Honda Shigetsuma]]''' (son of Tadashige Honda and uncle of Shigehara Honda), saw a new opportunity in 2016. The LDP government, led by [[Toshiro Kurosawa]], was deeply unpopular and collapsed due to the [[Paraña Bank Scandal]] and an internal leadership crisis.

In the [[Okaiken general election, 2016|2016 general election]], the PPO joined a "left-wing" coalition with the [[Sanese Communist Party|SCP]], [[Okaiken Socialist Party|OSP]], and [[Social Democratic Party (Okaiken)|SDP]]. The coalition successfully ousted the LDP, but the SCP's "meteoric rise" made them the largest party. The PPO entered government as a major coalition partner to SCP Prime Minister [[Sho Aoyagi]].

The Aoyagi government struggled with high inflation (6.8% in 2020) and a series of political gaffes. Seeing an opportunity, Honda and the PPO distanced themselves from their more radical coalition partners. In the [[Okaiken general election, 2021|2021 general election]], the PPO ran on a platform of "Stable Progress," positioning itself as a competent, centrist alternative to both the "reckless" SCP and the "fractured" LDP.

The strategy was a massive success. The PPO gained 70 seats to become the largest party with 201 seats, while the SCP and LDP suffered heavy losses. Honda Shigetsuma was appointed Prime Minister, forming a PPO-led minority government with confidence and supply support from the [[New Komeito Party|NKP]] and [[Social Democratic Party (Okaiken)|SDP]]. His first term was defined by the popular but costly [[National Universal Health Act]] of 2023.

In the [[Okaiken general election, 2025|2025 general election]], the PPO's campaign was criticized as "smug," and the party lost 20 seats. However, it remained the largest party in the Diet with 181 seats. Lacking a majority, Honda negotiated a new coalition, this time with the newly resurgent [[Okaiken Socialist Party|OSP]], and remained Prime Minister.

==Ideology and Policies==
The PPO is a centre-left party grounded in [[wikipedia:Social Democracy|Social Democracy]]. Its platform is generally more moderate than that of the Sanese Communist Party or the Okaiken Socialist Party.

* '''Economy:''' The party advocates for a [[wikipedia:Social market economy|social market economy]], supporting a strong social safety net funded by a progressive tax system. It is generally seen as pragmatic and pro-business, as seen in its 2021 "Stable Progress" platform, which contrasted with the SCP's calls for nationalization.
* '''Social Policy:''' The PPO is socially progressive, supporting public healthcare (as with the [[National Universal Health Act]]), education funding, and environmental protections. It also supports liberal immigration policies to address labor shortages.
* '''Foreign Policy:''' The PPO supports international cooperation and has historically been more pacifist than the LDP, though it maintains a pragmatic approach to national defense.

==List of Progressive Prime Ministers of Okaiken==
* [[Tadashige Honda]] (1961–1964)
* [[Shigehara Honda]] (1990–1991, 1991–1993)
* [[Honda Shigetsuma]] (2021–present)

